// Three scope-less `Read` requests log alice as their caller, ahead of alice's own `Read`. Under
// the strict mirror rule ingestion rejects them, so alice's first request is under her limit, and
// the specification allows it. Under its default rule, `MirrorRule::Strict`, the crate fails each
// forged request closed and does not record it, so it allows her request too. Under the opt-out
// `MirrorRule::Current`, which accepts any logged caller when the request side does not resolve,
// it would record them in alice's history and deny her request.
@id("read")
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"Read", resource);
@id("read_rate_limit")
forbid (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"Read", resource)
when temporal {
    (count for (t: Timepoint). where formerly within 1h (Drupe::Action::"Read"::request{} && tp(t))) > 2
};
